{
  "title": "Update EU database of processing factors",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "European Food Safety Authority"
    }
  ],
  "date": "2022-09",
  "abstract": "This document presents an update of the European Union (EU) database of processing factors, which are used to estimate pesticide residues in processed commodities.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Introduction",
      "text": "The EU database of processing factors is a critical tool for estimating pesticide residues in processed commodities. This document presents an update of the database, which includes new studies and improvements to data quality."
    },
    {
      "title": "Methodology",
      "text": "The update was conducted using a combination of manual and automated methods. The database was extended with respect to considered processes and processed commodities, while for some commodities it was decided to not include them."
    },
    {
      "title": "Results",
      "text": "The updated database includes 123 new processing studies, which were evaluated according to integrated quality parameters. Several processing factors have been marked as “not acceptable” or just as “indicative”."
    },
    {
      "title": "Discussion",
      "text": "The study data quality is quite heterogeneous, partly due to very different points in time where the studies have been originally conducted (1969-2020). Some were conducted before the respective OECD Guideline 508 became available."
    },
    {
      "title": "Recommendations",
      "text": [
        "Establish a mechanism for regular updates of the EU database of processing factors.",
        "Develop a suitable workflow for the extraction of processing studies from different regulatory procedures.",
        "Explore other sources for processing studies, such as national/zonal authorisation procedures for plant protection products in EU Member States."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "title": "ESA (online)",
      "url": ""
    },
    {
      "title": "BNN (2012)",
      "url": ""
    }
  ]
}
```

