{"summary": "Here is a JSON representation of the text:

```
{
  "title": "Update EU database of processing factors",
  "authors": [
    "European Food Safety Authority"
  ],
  "date": "2022-09",
  "abstract": "This document presents an update to the European Union (EU) database of processing factors, which are used to estimate pesticide residues in processed commodities. The update includes new studies and revisions to existing data, as well as improvements to the database's quality control procedures.",
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "text": "Establish a mechanism for regular updates of the EU database of processing factors",
      "description": "New studies are conducted and submitted continuously, and residue definitions keep changing."
    },
    {
      "text": "Align raw commodity categories used with respect to storage stability and analytical methods",
      "description": "This should be kept in mind when updating the respective OECD guideline and guidance document."
    },
    {
      "text": "Improve transparency and traceability of processing studies underlying a PF",
      "description": "Unambiguous study citations (title, author, year, study number) were often missing for processing studies evaluated in EFSA's Reasoned Opinions and in the underlying Evaluation Reports."
    }
  ],
  "database_updates": [
    {
      "text": "Added new processing studies to the existing data pool",
      "description": "The database was extended with respect to considered processes and processed commodities, while for some commodities it was decided to not include them."
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved database quality",
      "description": "Several processing factors have been marked as “not acceptable” or just as “indicative”, providing support for database users."
    }
  ],
  "future_work": [
    {
      "text": "Establish a set of quality criteria for generic drying factors",
      "description": "A list of suitable factors should be provided together with recommendations for extrapolation."
    },
    {
      "text": "Explore other sources for processing studies, such as national/zonal authorisation procedures and self-monitoring in food processing industry",
      "description": "This would provide a valuable source of real-world processing factors, beyond laboratory-scale experiments."
    }
  ]
}
```

Note that this is not an exhaustive representation of the text, but rather a selection of key points and recommendations.", "dataset_name": "European database of processing factors for pesticides residues in food", "source_length": 70953, "full_source_length": 70953, "num_context_blocks": 0, "extraction_strategy": "keyword"}

